infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title Where the 200 ms goes — London to California
  desc The physics floor is fixed; code cannot shrink it. Only moving content closer can.
  order asc
  sequences
    - label One-way light in fiber ~43 ms
      desc 8,700 km at ~200,000 km/s in glass — the hard physical floor. No optimisation goes below it.
    - label Round-trip light only ~87 ms
      desc The signal must go there and back before the first byte returns. Still pure physics, still unbeatable.
    - label + TCP + TLS + queuing ~200-250 ms
      desc Real handshakes and buffering stack on top of the light-speed round-trip. This is what the user actually feels.
    - label Edge cache hit instead ~10-20 ms
      desc A CDN serves from a POP 20 ms away — 10-20x faster, by shortening the distance, not the network.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #6366f1 #10b981
